messages:
maria: Hey team — quick Helm question. We're trying to "splat" a bunch of keys into a ConfigMap from .Values.config (base) + .Values.overrides (user/Terraform). Problem: when Terraform renders an empty overrides it becomes `null` or `""` and ends up clobbering values or causing template errors. Anyone solved a safe deep-merge pattern in chart templates?

aj: We hit this too. Important notes: 1) Sprig's `merge` is shallow. 2) You need to defend against `null`/empty-string from TF. Our helper approach was to default empty overrides to an empty map and then do a small recursive merge helper. Example (simplified):

```
{{- define "helpers.deepMerge" -}}
{{- $a := index . 0 -}}
{{- $b := index . 1 -}}
{{- range $k, $v := $b -}}
  {{- if and (kindIs "map" $v) (kindIs "map" (index $a $k)) -}}
    {{- $_ := set $a $k (include "helpers.deepMerge" (list (index $a $k) $v)) -}}
  {{- else -}}
    {{- $_ := set $a $k $v -}}
  {{- end -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $a -}}
{{- end -}}
```

Call it like: `{{- $merged := include "helpers.deepMerge" (list .Values.config (default dict .Values.overrides)) }}`. That `default dict` avoids `null`/`""`.

kevin: Nice. Two small additions: 1) Terraform side — if you can, make the module emit `{}` instead of `null` for empty maps (eg `tomap({})` or conditional in the template). 2) In Helm templates you can also guard with `{{- $ov := default dict .Values.overrides }}` and then `if gt (len $ov) 0` before merging to avoid unnecessary work.

sara: Also fyi: if this ConfigMap is used with `envFrom`, a nil/empty map can produce an `envFrom` section with no items which some linters flag. I usually render `envFrom` conditionally: `{{- if gt (len $merged) 0 }}
  envFrom:
  - configMapRef:
      name: {{ $name }}
{{- end }}`. Keeps manifests tidy.

maria: Great — thanks. One follow-up: our TF pipeline currently writes a `values.json` via `templatefile` and then uploads to S3. When `overrides` is absent the key is present but set to `""` in some modules. Any quick in-chart fix to coerce that to a map?

aj: Use `default dict` as above. `default` will treat empty string as a value, though, so you might want `coalesce`-style behavior. Helm doesn't have `coalesce`, but you can do something like: `{{- $raw := .Values.overrides }}
{{- if or (eq $raw "") (eq $raw nil) }}{{- $overrides := dict }}{{- else }}{{- $overrides := $raw }}{{- end }}` — clunky but works. Alternatively pre-process the JSON (sed/ jq) in the TF pipeline: `jq 'if .overrides == "" then .overrides = {} else . end' values.json`.

deploy-bot: deploy-bot posted a status update: linting/staging/chart-name v2.3.7 — all checks passed :white_check_mark:

kevin: :thumbsup: Can someone add a chart-test case for the empty-overrides scenario? Catches regressions.

sara: I'll add a `values-empty-overrides.yaml` to chart-tests and assert no `envFrom` block is generated and that ConfigMap has merged keys. Dropping a PR later today.

maria: Awesome, thanks everyone — will try the helper + TF tweak and report back. @aj @sara please ping me on the PR if you see anything weird. :pray:
